  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal contract obligations in Michigan are $5.8B for FY2026 to date. Procurement activity reached 163,993 awards with an average award size of $35.1K. Obligations fell 12.8% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $2.9B. The General Services Administration is the second largest buyer, obligating $1.9B. Automobile Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $1.8B, while Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing follows at $1.4B. GENERAL DYNAMICS LAND SYSTEMS INC. is the top vendor with $1.4B in obligations. Auto OEMs occupy several top-vendor slots: FORD MOTOR CO at $648M, GENERAL MOTORS LLC at $643M, and FCA US LLC at $525M. Year-to-date obligations to smaller agencies and industries include the Department of Veterans Affairs at $230M, Department of Homeland Security at $228M, Petroleum Refineries at $152M, and AVFUEL CORP at $152M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal buying in Michigan?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $2.9B, so defense buying accounts for a large share of Michigan obligations. The General Services Administration obligated $1.9B, meaning two agencies dominate the top buyer list. The remaining top buyers range from $230M down to $28.2M, showing a steep drop after the leading agencies."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors drive Michigan contract dollars?",
        "body": "Automobile Manufacturing is the largest industry with $1.8B in obligations, and Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing follows with $1.4B. GENERAL DYNAMICS LAND SYSTEMS INC. is the top vendor with $1.4B, and major automakers FORD MOTOR CO, GENERAL MOTORS LLC, and FCA US LLC together hold substantial obligations. Several specialized suppliers and service firms appear in the top ten, including AVFUEL CORP at $152M and ROLLs-ROYCE SOLUTIONS AMERICA INC at $104M."
      }
    ]
  },
